TEXT 136 16 Left 3 ;#197 The V-I curve the tracer is drawing
TEXT 136 80 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WWY-pakm_OM
TEXT 136 128 Left 2 ;Sweeping a source straight across the same 1N4148 plots its current against its own
TEXT 136 160 Left 2 ;terminal voltage, which is the curve the X-Y display is trying to trace.
TEXT 640 240 Left 2 !.dc VSWEEP -5 0.82 2m
TEXT 640 280 Left 2 !.meas dc ID_AT_816MV FIND I(D1) AT 0.816
TEXT 136 496 Left 2 ;This is not a circuit from the video. With no 50 ohm source and no shunt in the loop,
TEXT 136 528 Left 2 ;the horizontal axis carries the diode's own voltage and nothing else. Comparing it with
TEXT 136 560 Left 2 ;the tracer's numbers shows how far the shunt shifts the measured curve sideways.
